list.item:
Lemnitzer, General Lyman L., Vice Chief of
                        Staff, U.S. Army, until July 1959; Chief of Staff, July 1959–September 1960;
                        thereafter Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff

person.note:
First Secretary of Embassy in the United Kingdom through September 1958;
                    Director of the Office of Chinese Affairs, Bureau of Far Eastern Affairs,
                    Department of State, from September 1958

Assistant Secretary of State for European Affairs, November 1958–August 1959;
                    Deputy Undersecretary of State for Political Affairs, August–December 1959;
                    thereafter Under Secretary of State for Political Affairs

Vice Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of China through 1959;
                    Ambassador to Spain, 1959–June 1960; thereafter Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs

Ambassador of the People’s Republic of China to Poland, 1958–1960;
                    Representative of the People’s Republic of China in Ambassadorial talks with the
                    United States from September 1958
